{"id": "P00189", "name": "Dang Yanbao", "name_chinese": "党彦宝", "country": "China", "net_worth_usd_m": "19837.9", "net_worth_source": "Forbes real-time", "source_of_wealth": "Coal", "industry": "metals & mining", "sec_insider_companies": "", "shared_with": "", "appears_on": "Forbes real-time (2026); Forbes annual (2018-2025); Hurun Global (2018-2026); Hurun China (2014-2026)", "focus": ["energy"], "forbes_profile_url": "https://www.forbes.com/profile/dang-yanbao/", "wikidata_url": "", "forbes_bio": ["Dang Yanbao is the chairman of Ningxia Baofeng Energy Group, a supplier of coal chemical products.", "He worked in building materials and investment before setting up Baofeng Energy in 2005.", "Another private firm, Baofeng Energy Storage, began trial production at its 100GWh battery and energy-storage plant in northwestern China's Yinchuan city in 2024.", "In 2025, Baofeng Energy began operations at a $6.7 billion olefins plant in Inner Mongolia, one of the world's largest, raising the company's annual capacity for olefin to 5.2 million tons."], "forbes_facts": []}
{"id": "P01229", "name": "Paul Foster", "name_chinese": "Paul Foster", "country": "United States", "net_worth_usd_m": "5424.5", "net_worth_source": "Forbes real-time", "source_of_wealth": "Oil refining", "industry": "energy", "sec_insider_companies": "", "shared_with": "", "appears_on": "Forbes real-time (2026); Forbes annual (2008-2025); Hurun Global (2014-2026); Wikidata (2025)", "focus": ["energy"], "forbes_profile_url": "https://www.forbes.com/profile/paul-foster/", "wikidata_url": "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q136480371", "forbes_bio": ["Texas-based Paul Foster built a fortune in oil refining.", "In 2017, he sold his company Western Refining to San Antonio-based Tesoro for $6.4 billion. The merged entity was later renamed Andeavor and sold to Marathon Petroleum.", "Through Franklin Mountain Investments, Foster owns stakes in more than 30 companies spanning real estate, restaurants and sports. In 2025, he sold his energy venture for $2.5 billion.", "A graduate of Baylor University and a registered CPA, Foster handled the books for small oil refineries across the Southwest.", "He and his partners took over bankrupt El Paso Refining in 1992. He bought out his partners five years later.", "Foster serves as a trustee of the Baylor College of Medicine and is a member of the Texas Parks and Wildlife Commission and the Federal Reserve Bank of Dallas' Energy Advisory Council."], "forbes_facts": ["Foster is a part owner of the El Paso Chihuahuas, a Triple-A baseball team."]}
